### Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe the problem.

A layout using Blazor sections may need to render a wrapper only when a page supplies content, or use different markup for the page's content and the default. `SectionOutlet` does not expose whether it has a provider or let the outlet wrap its content, so wrapper markup may need to be repeated in producers or rendered even when the section is empty.

### Describe the solution you'd like

Expose content presence and allow the layout to wrap the active section content. One possible shape is a templated outlet (illustrative, not a finalized API):

```razor
<SectionOutlet SectionName="MobileTitle">
    <ChildContent Context="section">
        @if (section.HasContent)
        {
            <span class="title-override">@section.Content</span>
        }
        else
        {
            <span class="title-default"><DocumentTitleViewer /></span>
        }
    </ChildContent>
</SectionOutlet>
```

Here `HasContent` would mean a matching content provider is active, not that its fragment produced nonempty HTML. The presence and wrapping APIs and their interaction with fallback content need design. A query service or cascading value is another option for detecting presence, although wrapping the content would still need a mechanism of its own.

### Additional context

In my Recollections app, the [`MobileTitle` placeholder in the layout](https://github.com/neptuo/Recollections/blob/ffb9a480d25612e164c1ae838acc118be4d11644/src/Recollections.Blazor.UI/Commons/Layouts/HeadLayout.razor) uses different wrappers for provided content and the fallback:

```razor
<TemplatePlaceholder Name="MobileTitle">
    <ChildContent Context="contents">
        <span class="navbar-text text-white py-0 fs-4 d-sm-none flex-grow-1 me-auto">
            @foreach (var content in contents)
            {
                @content.ChildContent
            }
        </span>
    </ChildContent>
    <EmptyContent>
        <span class="navbar-text text-white py-0 fs-4 d-sm-none flex-grow-1 overflow-hidden text-truncate me-auto">
            <DocumentTitleViewer />
        </span>
    </EmptyContent>
</TemplatePlaceholder>
```

The [placeholder implementation](https://github.com/neptuo/Recollections/blob/ffb9a480d25612e164c1ae838acc118be4d11644/src/Recollections.Blazor.Components/Components/TemplatePlaceholder.cs) chooses the empty content or invokes the supplied wrapper template:

```csharp
if (content.Count == 0)
{
    builder.AddContent(0, EmptyContent);
    return;
}

if (ChildContent != null)
{
    builder.AddContent(0, ChildContent(content));
    return;
}
```

Pages supply the content without the layout's wrapper, for example [Calendar](https://github.com/neptuo/Recollections/blob/ffb9a480d25612e164c1ae838acc118be4d11644/src/Recollections.Blazor.UI/Entries/Pages/Calendar.razor):

```razor
<TemplateContent Name="MobileTitle">Calendar</TemplateContent>
```

[InlineTitleEdit](https://github.com/neptuo/Recollections/blob/ffb9a480d25612e164c1ae838acc118be4d11644/src/Recollections.Blazor.UI/Entries/Components/InlineTitleEdit.razor) also supplies an interactive override. The override wrapper omits the fallback's truncation classes.

My Money app's [layout](https://github.com/maraf/Money/blob/1b49fcd2b114c74f0423b4b1eeefa4bb1f20d8b7/src/Money.Blazor.Host/Layouts/Layout.razor) and [Title component](https://github.com/maraf/Money/blob/1b49fcd2b114c74f0423b4b1eeefa4bb1f20d8b7/src/Money.Blazor.Host/Components/Title.razor) offer a possible use for conditional layout wrappers and a header spacer, although that refactoring has not been tried and the spacer also depends on the title's `Sub` value.

Related: #52477 asks how to detect whether a section has content. This issue also asks for outlet-side wrapping; the illustrated API has not been prototyped.

